      "For a suspected fuel or chemical release, avoid ignition sources and do not touch or walk through the liquid. Identify placards or cargo information only from a safe position; give responders the product/UN number if known, without approaching to investigate.",
      "For EV/hybrid incidents, identify the vehicle type from a safe distance when possible. Damaged orange high-voltage cables, battery smoke, hissing, popping, unusual heat or re-ignition risk require isolation and specialist fire response; do not cut high-voltage components.",
