      "When a vehicle has contacted an overhead line, treat it and the surrounding ground as energized until the utility or competent electrical authority confirms otherwise. Keep people away, prevent approach, and follow the electrical emergency plan.",
      "Night or low-visibility response needs approved lighting that does not blind drivers, clear perimeter control, high-visibility PPE, and a protected working area. Hand signals alone are not a substitute for the site traffic plan.",
