      'Document isolation points, locks, verification, rescue decisions, tools used, injuries, machine condition, witnesses and restart authorization. Preserve evidence without compromising safety.',
      'Before restart: investigate, repair, test guards/interlocks, review risk assessment and procedure, brief affected workers and obtain formal release from responsible management.',
      "Keep machine isolation instructions at or readily accessible from the equipment, with an up-to-date diagram identifying every energy-isolating device and stored-energy release point.",
      "Conduct a pre-task rescue review for unusual maintenance, jam clearing, cleaning, confined access or work where a person could be caught. Confirm rescue tools can reach the casualty without exposing rescuers.",
      "After rescue, quarantine the machine and tag it out of service. Record lock numbers/owners and do not remove controls until the formal site procedure permits it.",
